{"id":"q54","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"fact","question":"Is the Mona Lisa painted on canvas?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The Mona Lisa is not painted on canvas.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The Mona Lisa is oil paint on a poplar wood panel of roughly 77 × 53 cm.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The Louvre, which holds the painting, documents the panel support.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Many famous paintings, especially from later centuries, are on canvas.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The word 'painting' often suggests canvas, making the assumption of canvas understandable.","confidence":0.7,"lean":1,"theta":1.0996,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Some Renaissance works used canvas, so assuming canvas is not unreasonable.","confidence":0.7,"lean":1,"theta":1.0996,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Leonardo da Vinci worked on panel for this portrait.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Conservation and art-historical records describe the poplar support, including wood grain and preparation as physical evidence.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Nothing in the record points to canvas.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The general association of paintings with canvas does not outweigh the specific evidence of a panel.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":9,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,